# Where the built site is mounted. Leave unset for a domain apex.
#
# Set this ONLY if you are hosting under a sub-path:
#   example.com/form/            ->  PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/form/
#   user.github.io/my-repo/      ->  PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/my-repo/
#
# It must end with a slash, and it must match on both sides: Vite uses it for
# asset URLs (vite.config.ts) and React Router uses it as its basename
# (src/main.tsx, via import.meta.env.BASE_URL).
#
# Copy this file to `.env.production` and uncomment the line you need, then
# rebuild. Leaving it unset is correct and needs no file at all.
#
# PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/form/
